      {
        "id": 139522,
        "name": "MigrantP",
        "username": "MigrantP",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/{size}/1921_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-15T20:37:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Also:</p>\n<blockquote>Shock Rounds text is adjusted to say “The first time that card’s power is used to damage a target, Expatriette deals each non-hero target 1 lightning damage. After that power is used, destroy this card.” This clarifies that the lightning damage only happens once.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nOkay, I know what you want, but that is still ambiguous. What if I read it that \"the first time that card's power is used to damage a target - on a&nbsp;<em>per target</em> basis, ...\" a la the way Combat Stance and Flame Barrier are supposed to work? It might be better to say \"the first time&nbsp;<em>each</em> target\" vs \"the first time&nbsp;<em>any</em> target,\" or some wording that adds disambiguity. Or even, \"The first time..., Expariette deals each non-hero target 1 lighting damage, then destroy this card.\"Shock Rounds have been in our house rules for a while, because while Expatriette is an awesomely reliable dealer of small amounts of damage, she doesn't really have any awesome game-changing slam-dunk moves. So we let her Shock Rounds re-trigger.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Personally I thought the original wording was fine and unambiguous (with the exact same interpretation, that the lightning damage only happens once). I'll bring this back to Christopher.</p>",
        "post_number": 71,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:16:15.841Z",
