      {
        "id": 139523,
        "name": "MigrantP",
        "username": "MigrantP",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/{size}/1921_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-15T20:38:14.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Matchstickman\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/48/1880_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Matchstickman:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Hmmmmmmm. I don't know if it's a consequence of this</p>\n<div>Quote:<br><blockquote>When a card enters play, the following order of things occurs.&nbsp;Ongoing effects on the card become applicable.Cards that react to other cards entering play now act.One-time effects on the card happen.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nor not but the Mask of the Matriarch is triggering off itself entering play, I really don't think that's how it's meant to work.&nbsp;EDIT: Ronway tested this for me, seems like it's not rules ambiquity but a bug!<a href=\"http://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=425298440\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">pic1</a><a href=\"http://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=425300556\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">pic2</a><a href=\"http://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=425300609\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">pic3</a><a href=\"http://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=425300651\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">pic4</a>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's a bug. Fixed in the next update.</p>",
