      {
        "id": 139526,
        "name": "MigrantP",
        "username": "MigrantP",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/{size}/1921_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-15T20:47:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>'k.</p>\n<p>Seems like we are getting more and more card-specific rulings that might run against the overall general rulings. At least that phenomenon must be obvious to MigrantP… I wonder how big his if-else structures are getting!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not really. Almost always we are aiming to discern a rule that is consistent between many cards, and that's what comes out.</p>\n<p>And that's not how we program =)</p>",
