      {
        "id": 139529,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-16T01:58:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MigrantP\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/48/1921_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MigrantP:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Trajector wrote:</b><br>\n<blockquote>Wooooaaaah.And this puts some arguments to rest, doesn't it?Quote:<br>\n<blockquote>Jack Handle effectively cancels the original damage, and causes a new set of damage dealing instance to all non-hero targets with the original damage amount/type/irreducibility. \n</blockquote>\n<p>…or does it? Can Fixer double-dip Grease Monkey’s +1?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>I’m not sure what you’re asking here.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I was trying to ask at what point does the Jack Handle cancel the original attack and determine how much “that much” damage is. Is it before or after damage modifiers apply?</p>\n<p>If it was after the modifiers, you could get some similar effects to the dual crowbar.</p>\n<p>Someone answered me above - at least, they answered what happens.</p>",
        "post_number": 78,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:16:16.400Z",
